note Exercism-style exercise "bob": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/bob
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note response writes Bob's reply to s into o and returns its length. Silence (only spaces, tabs,
note CR, LF): "Fine. Be that way!". A yelled question: "Calm down, I know what I'm doing!". Yelling
note (some letter, no lower-case letter): "Whoa, chill out!". A question (last non-space byte is
note "?"): "Sure.". Anything else: "Whatever.".
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/bob
om2
text bfine "Fine. Be that way!"
text bcalm "Calm down, I know what I'm doing!"
text bwhoa "Whoa, chill out!"
text bsure "Sure."
text bwhat "Whatever."
fn app o edit uchar * p ulong s view uchar * to ulong
q = p
for i ulong len s
put o q get s i
q = add q 1
end
ret q
end
fn lastbyte s view uchar * to uchar
last = uchar 0
for i ulong len s
c = get s i
if not or or or eq c 32 eq c 9 eq c 10 eq c 13
last = c
end
end
ret last
end
fn hasrange s view uchar * lo uchar hi uchar to bool
for i ulong len s
c = get s i
if and ge c lo le c hi
ret true
end
end
ret false
end
fn response s view uchar * o edit uchar * to ulong
last = lastbyte s
up = hasrange s 65 90
lo = hasrange s 97 122
if eq last 0
ret app o 0 bfine
end
yell = and up not lo
q = eq last 63
if and yell q
ret app o 0 bcalm
end
if yell
ret app o 0 bwhoa
end
if q
ret app o 0 bsure
end
ret app o 0 bwhat
end
